% Problem 37. Chace vol. II pl. 59 (photographs XIV-XV, register 3), PDF pp. 165-166; Peet pp. 74-75 (Pl. M).
No. 37
{"Go down I times 3 into the hekat-measure, '3 of me is added to me, '3 of '3 of me is added to me, '9 of me is added to me; return I, filled am I."}
{"Then what says it?"} {"Shall hear it:"}   % Chace fn 1: "That is, Let it hear"; Peet: "Let it hear"
% the first column: the papyrus's multipliers are 1, 2, '3, "'3 of '3 of it" and "'9 of it", which last two the notation cannot hold as multipliers; so the products are written one to a line and the multipliers kept in notes
1         % 1
2         % 2
'3        % '3
'9        % "'3 of '3 of it"
'9        % "'9 of it"
{Total 3 '2 '18.}
Reckon with 3 '2 '18 to find 1.     % "Call 1 out of 3 '2 '18." (Peet: "Divide 1 by 3 '2 '18")
  1      3 '2 '18
  '2     1 '2 '4 36             % 36 for '36: Chace fn 2: "The scribe omitted the fractional dots in these places."
\ '4     '2 '4 '8 '72
  '8     '4 '8 '16 '144
  '16    '8 '16 32 '288         % 32 for '32 (Chace fn 2)
\ '32    '16 '32 '64 '576
{Total 1.}
"Add '2 '4 '8 '72 '16 '32 '64 '576"   % "km" (Peet: "Addition", literally "completion"); '2 '4 '8 are left out of the sum, which is of the last five
"{8 36 18 9 1}"                       % red, beneath '72 '16 '32 '64 '576: values in 576ths. Chace's translation page prints the second as what looks like 35 (a broken 6); Chace's plate glosses the hieratic as 36 (written 63, right to left), and Peet has 36
'72
'16
'32
'64
'576
Total '8.                 % "dmd '8"; beneath it in red 72 (the five red values add to 72)
{"Example of proof."}
% the multipliers again 1, 2, "'3 of it", "'3 of '3 of it", "'9 of it"
'4 '32       % 1
'2 '16       % 2
'12 '96      % "'3 of it"
'36 '288     % "'3 of '3 of it"
'36 '288     % "'9 of it"
{Total 1.}
"{Add} '2 '4 '32 '16 '12 '96 '36 '288 '36 '288"   % "km" in red; '2 '4 left out of the sum
"{9 18 24 3 8 1 8 1}"                             % red, beneath the eight others: values in 288ths
'32
'16
'12
'96
'36
'288
'36
'288
Total '4.                 % "dmd '4"; beneath it in red 72
% the answer in ro, and the proof in ro beside the proof in hekat parts ("Making of grain")
"Total 320."              % "dmd 320" heading the column: the hekat, 320 ro
  '2     160
\ '4     80
  '8     40
  16     20               % 16 for '16: Chace fn 2: fractional dots omitted
\ 32     10               % 32 for '32 (Chace fn 2)
Total 90.
{"Example of proof."}
% ticks in the papyrus (Chace and Peet agree): \1 90, \2 180, '3 30 (no tick; Peet: sic), "'3 of '3" 10 (no tick; Peet: sic), \ "'9 of it" 10
90           % \ 1
180          % \ 2
30           % '3
10           % "'3 of '3"
10           % \ "'9 of it"
Total 320.
"Making of grain:"        % Peet: "amounting in corn to"; all five rows ticked
'4 '32 hekat     % \ 1
'2 '16 hekat     % \ 2
'16 '32 hekat    % \ '3
'32 hekat        % \ "'3 of '3"
'32 hekat        % \ "'9 of it"
Total '2 '8 '4 '8 hekat.  % written so, not largest first (Peet the same)
